*.sh text eol=lf

# board_run/*.hex (BR.4): committed prebuilt firmware, pinned byte for byte
# by board_run/SHA256SUMS.txt. Without this, core.autocrlf=true silently
# turns the toolchain's CRLF line endings into LF on `git add` (found while
# staging A-EV74H48A-b41af3b.hex: the blob came out 5702 bytes - one per
# line - smaller than the file actually built) and the exact bytes on a
# colleague's checkout would then depend on THEIR core.autocrlf/core.eol,
# not on what is committed. "binary" disables every text/eol/diff
# conversion, so the file round-trips identically everywhere.
*.hex binary
